 "note": "Every lunar eclipse from 2025 to 2030. Type, Terrestrial Dynamical Time of greatest eclipse, Delta T, gamma, magnitudes and phase durations are the rows of the catalogue page. Contact times are those printed on each eclipse's figure (P1/P4: the Moon's limb touches the penumbra; U1/U4: the umbra; U2/U3: the whole Moon is inside the umbra), in Universal Time as NASA gives them, that is Dynamical Time minus NASA's predicted Delta T. The figures are images: the times were transcribed from them and checked against the catalogue durations (P4 - P1, U4 - U1, U3 - U2 agree to the 0.1 minute printed). Shadow rule: Danjon. Ephemerides: VSOP87/ELP2000-85. Values are NASA's, unmodified.",
